1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:07,412
Before a jet engine ever carries passengers, it must prove that it can survive some of the most extreme conditions in engineering.

2
00:00:07,362 --> 00:00:12,475
Inside the engine, thousands of components work together at incredible speeds.

3
00:00:12,475 --> 00:00:18,362
Air enters through the massive fan, passes through the compressor, and reaches the combustion chamber.

4
00:00:18,362 --> 00:00:24,425
Here, fuel ignites, releasing energy that drives the turbine and produces the thrust needed for flight.

5
00:00:24,425 --> 00:00:30,475
During testing, engineers monitor temperature, pressure, vibration, and rotational speed.

6
00:00:30,475 --> 00:00:32,787
Every measurement matters.

7
00:00:32,787 --> 00:00:36,950
Because at thirty thousand feet, there is no room for failure.

